01:43:38.653 --> 01:43:40.855
<i>over Enson Inoue</i>
<i>in the first round,</i>

2096
01:43:40.955 --> 01:43:42.890
<i>and he looks to keep</i>
<i>his good fortune going</i>

2097
01:43:42.990 --> 01:43:46.094
<i>with a win against</i>
<i>one of the toughest fighters</i>

2098
01:43:46.194 --> 01:43:47.394
<i>in the division.</i>

2099
01:43:47.494 --> 01:43:50.531
<i>Will Kerr silence</i>
<i>his critics here with a win?</i>

2100
01:43:50.631 --> 01:43:54.168
<i>Or will all his hopes</i>
<i>and dreams come crashing down?</i>

2101
01:43:54.267 --> 01:43:56.871
<i>If Kerr is in any way</i>
<i>similar to the man</i>

2102
01:43:56.971 --> 01:43:58.305
<i>I know he is,</i>

2103
01:43:58.405 --> 01:44:00.508
<i>he will want to win this fight</i>

2104
01:44:00.608 --> 01:44:02.977
<i>and tournament</i>
<i>more than life itself.</i>

2105
01:44:03.077 --> 01:44:05.245
(THRILLING MUSIC PLAYING)

2106
01:44:11.219 --> 01:44:13.955
All right. Ready? Fight.

2107
01:44:25.166 --> 01:44:26.868
Close the bars. Nice job.

2108
01:44:28.435 --> 01:44:29.937
Nice jabs on him.

2109
01:44:30.037 --> 01:44:31.806
(SPEAKS INDISTINCTLY)

2110
01:44:33.040 --> 01:44:34.609
Nice! Good job!

2111
01:44:36.677 --> 01:44:37.845
Yes! Nice!

2112
01:44:38.980 --> 01:44:40.480
Don't stop. Go push in.

2113
01:44:41.015 --> 01:44:42.517
Oh, jeez!

2114
01:44:44.384 --> 01:44:45.787
Yes! Get him back.

2115
01:44:46.386 --> 01:44:48.055
Yes! You got him back.

2116
01:44:52.894 --> 01:44:54.361
Let's go, let's go.

2117
01:44:54.461 --> 01:44:56.864
(FUJITA'S CORNERMAN
SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY)

2118
01:45:03.237 --> 01:45:04.672
That's illegal.

2119
01:45:04.772 --> 01:45:06.974
Mark, get out
of this situation.

2120
01:45:07.074 --> 01:45:08.375
Just get up, man.

2121
01:45:10.477 --> 01:45:12.013
Yes, take your time.
Take your time.

2122
01:45:12.113 --> 01:45:13.614
Move around. Take a breath.

2123
01:45:14.682 --> 01:45:16.851
(THRILLING MUSIC CONTINUES)

2124
01:45:18.219 --> 01:45:20.621
-(SPEAKING JAPANESE)
-Come on, Mark.

2125
01:45:22.557 --> 01:45:24.525
BAS: (EXCLAIMS) Nice one.

2126
01:45:26.027 --> 01:45:27.795
Yeah! Uh-oh.

2127
01:45:27.895 --> 01:45:29.030
Nice job!

2128
01:45:30.363 --> 01:45:31.933
Nice! Oy!

2129
01:45:32.033 --> 01:45:34.367
Good job, good job.
Take your time. Relax.

2130
01:45:35.036 --> 01:45:36.604
Breathe in.

2131
01:45:37.470 --> 01:45:38.973
Take that takedown.

2132
01:45:41.209 --> 01:45:42.643
Come on, Mark.

2133
01:45:43.711 --> 01:45:44.712
Get up.

2134
01:45:46.614 --> 01:45:47.949
(MAN SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY)

2135
01:45:48.049 --> 01:45:49.851
Mark!

2136
01:45:49.951 --> 01:45:52.019
You got to improve
your position, Mark.

2137
01:45:54.088 --> 01:45:55.089
Come on!

2138
01:45:56.524 --> 01:45:58.993
<i>Lower your back so you can</i>
<i>see him coming at least.</i>

2139
01:46:01.428 --> 01:46:03.798
<i>Get up, Mark.</i>
<i>Watch out for his knees.</i>

2140
01:46:03.898 --> 01:46:07.367
<i>Improve your position.</i>
<i>Improve your position.</i>

2141
01:46:07.467 --> 01:46:09.003
Come on, Mark! Come on.

2142
01:46:10.671 --> 01:46:11.939
-(MARK GRUNTS)
-(BELL RINGING)

2143
01:46:12.039 --> 01:46:15.209
STEPHEN QUADROS: <i>Oh, my</i>
<i>goodness! Kerr has lost.</i>

2144
01:46:15.309 --> 01:46:17.511
<i>He is out of the tournament.</i>

2145
01:46:17.612 --> 01:46:21.481
<i>This has to be the first</i>
<i>major upset of the evening.</i>

2146
01:46:23.651 --> 01:46:26.921
<i>I have no idea what happened</i>
<i>to Mark out there.</i>

2147
01:46:27.755 --> 01:46:29.924
<i>He just couldn't move.</i>

2148
01:46:30.024 --> 01:46:31.325
<i>This is truly shocking.</i>

2149
01:46:31.424 --> 01:46:32.793
All right. Get up, Mark.

2150
01:46:32.894 --> 01:46:34.494
STEPHEN QUADROS: <i>One thing</i>
<i>I have to call attention to</i>

2151
01:46:34.595 --> 01:46:35.997
<i>is Mark's heart,</i>

2152
01:46:36.097 --> 01:46:38.032
<i>because we have seen a lot</i>
<i>of tap outs</i>

2153
01:46:38.132 --> 01:46:39.200
<i>in this tournament.</i>

2154
01:46:39.300 --> 01:46:40.868
<i>But Mark fell on his sword</i>

2155
01:46:40.968 --> 01:46:43.436
<i>in front of these</i>
<i>thousands of fans.</i>

2156
01:46:43.537 --> 01:46:46.007
<i>And for them,</i>
<i>he would rather be beaten</i>

2157
01:46:46.107 --> 01:46:47.241
<i>than quit.</i>

2158
01:46:47.341 --> 01:46:48.876
<i>I can tell you from experience</i>

2159
01:46:48.976 --> 01:46:51.112
<i>-that takes a true champion.</i>
-BAS: <i>Don't worry about it.</i>

2160
01:46:51.212 --> 01:46:52.513
I still love you, brother.

2161
01:46:52.613 --> 01:46:54.548
STEPHEN QUADROS: <i>Fujita moves</i>
<i>on to fight Mark Coleman</i>

2162
01:46:54.649 --> 01:46:57.318
<i>for a place in the final fight</i>
<i>of the evening</i>

2163
01:46:57.417 --> 01:46:58.653
<i>as we await the winner</i>

2164
01:46:58.753 --> 01:47:01.522
<i>of the Vovchanchyn</i>
<i>versus Sakuraba fight</i>

2165
01:47:01.622 --> 01:47:05.126
<i>and we get closer</i>
<i>to that $200,000 grand prize.</i>

2166
01:47:05.793 --> 01:47:07.962
(PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING)

2167
01:47:27.415 --> 01:47:28.683
Can we turn
the lights out, Bas?

2168
01:47:28.783 --> 01:47:30.418
Yeah, I'll take care of it.

2169
01:47:30.518 --> 01:47:32.253
I'm going to get you
some ice, too. Okay?

2170
01:47:32.353 --> 01:47:33.521
Yeah.

2171
01:47:34.255 --> 01:47:35.455
Hey, Mark.

2172
01:47:36.223 --> 01:47:37.825
Come here, big guy.

2173
01:47:37.925 --> 01:47:39.727
BAS: Raja, where
can I find some ice?

2174
01:47:40.261 --> 01:47:41.562
Over there.

2175
01:47:42.462 --> 01:47:43.764
How you doing, Mark?

2176
01:47:44.699 --> 01:47:46.334
BAS: All right, keep
your eyes closed

2177
01:47:46.434 --> 01:47:47.635
and put this on it.

2178
01:47:48.501 --> 01:47:50.137
Try to relax, all right?

2179
01:47:50.237 --> 01:47:51.238
(EXHALES)

2180
01:47:52.406 --> 01:47:54.976
-Mark, can you hear me?
-Yeah.

2181
01:47:55.076 --> 01:47:56.777
DR. CORTEZ: Do you know
what happened to you?

2182
01:47:56.877 --> 01:48:00.214
-Yeah, I lost.
-Yeah, you did.

2183
01:48:01.949 --> 01:48:03.451
Do you know
where you are right now?

2184
01:48:03.551 --> 01:48:06.153
-Japan.
-DR. CORTEZ: Good.

2185
01:48:06.754 --> 01:48:08.255
Do I need stitches?

2186
01:48:09.223 --> 01:48:10.758
Yeah, you need a few stitches.

2187
01:48:10.858 --> 01:48:13.194
-MARK: Is it bad?
-No, it's not horrible.

2188
01:48:15.296 --> 01:48:17.698
I'm just gonna go over here
and get everything ready.

2189
01:48:17.798 --> 01:48:19.433
All right? It'll be
a few minutes.

2190
01:48:19.533 --> 01:48:20.701
You just sit tight here.

2191
01:48:20.801 --> 01:48:22.770
-MARK: Yeah, okay.
-All right.

2192
01:48:23.671 --> 01:48:25.172
I could not move my body.

2193
01:48:25.272 --> 01:48:26.574
(BREATHES DEEPLY)

2194
01:48:26.674 --> 01:48:29.443
It's like I...
It was like I was dead.

2195
01:48:29.543 --> 01:48:31.979
Yep, I've been there, buddy.

2196
01:48:32.580 --> 01:48:33.848
I couldn't move.

2197
01:48:35.249 --> 01:48:36.684
Listen, Mark,
I hate to do this, brother,

2198
01:48:36.784 --> 01:48:38.886
but I gotta go back
to the commentary table, okay?

2199
01:48:38.986 --> 01:48:39.954
I gotta work.

2200
01:48:40.821 --> 01:48:42.857
-Okay.
-BAS: All right, man.

2201
01:48:42.957 --> 01:48:45.526
Bas, thank you.
Thank you for everything.

2202
01:48:47.028 --> 01:48:49.230
-BAS: You're welcome, brother.
-Yes.

2203
01:48:50.398 --> 01:48:51.932
-I'm sorry.
-BAS: No, no, no.

2204
01:48:52.033 --> 01:48:53.034
Don't say that.

2205
01:48:53.667 --> 01:48:54.869
Don't say that.

2206
01:48:58.539 --> 01:48:59.673
-You got him?
-I got him.

2207
01:48:59.774 --> 01:49:01.275
BAS: All right. Sounds good.

2208
01:49:12.153 --> 01:49:13.387
Hey, Doc.

2209
01:49:13.487 --> 01:49:14.455
Doc, sorry.

2210
01:49:14.555 --> 01:49:15.623
-Hey, Mark.
-How's Kerr?

2211
01:49:15.723 --> 01:49:16.924
He's okay. He's all right.

2212
01:49:17.024 --> 01:49:19.026
He got a gash here.
We gotta stitch that up.

2213
01:49:19.126 --> 01:49:20.494
How's his head?

2214
01:49:20.594 --> 01:49:22.263
-It's clearing up.
-Does he care if I go in?

2215
01:49:22.363 --> 01:49:23.431
-No, no, go in. Go in.
-Coleman.

2216
01:49:23.532 --> 01:49:25.199
COLEMAN: Thank you.
What's going on, bud?

2217
01:49:25.299 --> 01:49:26.867
MARK: Hey, man.

2218
01:49:26.967 --> 01:49:29.770
-How you feeling?
-(SIGHS) You know.

2219
01:49:30.304 --> 01:49:31.405
You all right?

2220
01:49:31.505 --> 01:49:32.640
Yeah, I'm a little banged up.

2221
01:49:32.740 --> 01:49:34.708
Nothing to worry
about, though.

2222
01:49:34.809 --> 01:49:37.411
Whatever. Let it go.
It happens.

2223
01:49:37.512 --> 01:49:39.080
It's one night.

2224
01:49:39.180 --> 01:49:40.481
We've all been there.

2225
01:49:40.581 --> 01:49:42.683
You heard about Fujita, right?

2226
01:49:42.783 --> 01:49:44.485
He's out.
He's not coming back.

2227
01:49:44.585 --> 01:49:45.619
He's injured.

2228
01:49:45.719 --> 01:49:47.621
Yeah, I know, I know.

2229
01:49:47.721 --> 01:49:49.290
It's all yours
to win now, Cole.

2230
01:49:50.491 --> 01:49:51.692
-For real?
-For real.

2231
01:49:51.792 --> 01:49:53.727
(BOTH CHUCKLING)

2232
01:49:53.828 --> 01:49:56.531
Yeah, buddy, it's all yours.
Go get it.

2233
01:49:56.664 --> 01:49:57.832
I'll fucking get it.

2234
01:49:57.932 --> 01:49:59.366
-MARK: It's all yours.
-Appreciate that.

2235
01:49:59.467 --> 01:50:00.935
-I love you, buddy.
-I love you.

2236
01:50:01.035 --> 01:50:02.103
-Go bring it home.
-I'll get it done.

2237
01:50:02.203 --> 01:50:03.572
STEPHEN QUADROS:
<i>So Mark Coleman is coming</i>

2238
01:50:03.671 --> 01:50:05.940
<i>into this final</i>
<i>looking fresh as ever</i>

2239
01:50:06.040 --> 01:50:07.908
<i>after his good friend,</i>
<i>Mark Kerr,</i>

2240
01:50:08.008 --> 01:50:09.743
<i>inadvertently did him a favor</i>

2241
01:50:09.844 --> 01:50:13.414
<i>after Fujita injured his knee</i>
<i>in their fight together.</i>

2242
01:50:13.515 --> 01:50:15.449
<i>The question is,</i>
<i>will Coleman be able</i>

2243
01:50:15.550 --> 01:50:18.219
<i>to avenge Kerr</i>
<i>against his nemesis,</i>

2244
01:50:18.319 --> 01:50:19.620
<i>Igor Vovchanchyn?</i>

2245
01:50:19.720 --> 01:50:21.556
<i>Or will Igor continue</i>
<i>his reign</i>

2246
01:50:21.655 --> 01:50:23.991
<i>as the top heavyweight</i>
<i>in the division?</i>

2247
01:50:24.091 --> 01:50:25.459
All right, Mark,
I'm gonna tell you

2248
01:50:25.560 --> 01:50:26.627
what I'm gonna do
every step of the way.

2249
01:50:26.727 --> 01:50:27.928
All right?

2250
01:50:28.028 --> 01:50:29.763
You just let me know
if anything is bothering you.

2251
01:50:29.864 --> 01:50:31.031
STEPHEN QUADROS:
<i>I should also note</i>

2252
01:50:31.132 --> 01:50:33.701
<i>this is the first time</i>
<i>a Pride event</i>

2253
01:50:33.801 --> 01:50:37.138
<i>has ever been broadcast</i>
<i>in North America.</i>

2254
01:50:37.238 --> 01:50:39.874
<i>And I think</i>
<i>they are in for a real treat.</i>

2255
01:50:39.974 --> 01:50:41.510
REFEREE: All right.
(SPEAKS INDISTINCTLY)

2256
01:50:41.610 --> 01:50:42.776
(BELL RINGS)

2257
01:50:43.811 --> 01:50:45.980
(CORNERMAN SPEAKING
INDISTINCTLY)

2258
01:50:46.881 --> 01:50:49.083
(MEN SHOUTING INDISTINCTLY)

2259
01:50:52.086 --> 01:50:53.821
You're gonna feel
a little pinch,

2260
01:50:53.921 --> 01:50:55.823
and then a lot of burning.

2261
01:50:56.957 --> 01:50:57.958
Pinch.

2262
01:50:58.859 --> 01:51:00.761
A lot of burning.

2263
01:51:02.263 --> 01:51:05.299
CORNERMAN: Take your time!
There you go! Yes!

2264
01:51:14.942 --> 01:51:17.678
Come on! Come on! Handle him!

2265
01:51:17.778 --> 01:51:19.947
Yes, yes, yes!
Spin him around! Spin him!

2266
01:51:20.047 --> 01:51:21.782
DR. CORTEZ: And two more.

2267
01:51:25.252 --> 01:51:27.254
CORNERMAN: Keep going!
Keep going!

2268
01:51:27.354 --> 01:51:28.923
Yes! Yes!

2269
01:51:29.558 --> 01:51:30.724
(IGOR GRUNTS)

2270
01:51:34.728 --> 01:51:35.664
STEPHEN QUADROS:
<i>There's the tap.</i>

2271
01:51:35.763 --> 01:51:37.831
<i>Wow! Igor has tapped out.</i>

2272
01:51:37.932 --> 01:51:41.135
<i>Mark Coleman has won</i>
<i>the Pride 2000 Grand Prix.</i>

2273
01:51:41.235 --> 01:51:43.237
<i>Oh! Look at the excitement</i>
<i>in that man.</i>

2274
01:51:43.337 --> 01:51:47.241
<i>He's crazy excited,</i>
<i>and he's running to the fans.</i>

2275
01:51:47.341 --> 01:51:49.076
<i>-He's running to the fans.</i>
-COLEMAN: <i>Yes!</i>

2276
01:51:49.176 --> 01:51:51.646
STEPHEN QUADROS:
<i>He just won $200,000.</i>

2277
01:51:51.745 --> 01:51:53.047
DR. CORTEZ:
All right. You're all done.

2278
01:51:53.147 --> 01:51:55.349
<i>(CORRIDOR OF DREAMS</i> PLAYING)

2279
01:52:00.454 --> 01:52:02.256
(CROWD CHEERING)

2280
01:52:10.965 --> 01:52:12.099
(MARK GRUNTS)

2281
01:53:23.504 --> 01:53:25.873
<i>(CORRIDOR OF DREAMS</i>
CONTINUES PLAYING)

2282
01:54:16.390 --> 01:54:18.359
(CHUCKLING)

2283
01:54:49.022 --> 01:54:50.725
-Hi, how are you?
-CASHIER: Hi.

2284
01:54:50.825 --> 01:54:53.127
(JAZZY MUSIC
PLAYING ON SPEAKERS)

2285
01:54:54.094 --> 01:54:55.530
-CASHIER: How are you?
-I'm good.

2286
01:54:55.630 --> 01:54:56.664
-Thank you.
-CASHIER: Good.

2287
01:54:56.765 --> 01:54:58.633
-How was your day so far?
-CASHIER: So far, so good.

2288
01:54:58.733 --> 01:55:00.000
-Yours?
-It's good.

2289
01:55:00.100 --> 01:55:02.069
-CASHIER: Good.
-Gonna get real busy.

2290
01:55:02.169 --> 01:55:04.004
-CASHIER: Yeah.
-(LAUGHS)

2291
01:55:04.104 --> 01:55:06.240
<i>(MAKE THE WORLD GO AWAY</i>
BY TIMI YURO PLAYING)

2292
01:55:25.660 --> 01:55:27.629
Uh... (CHUCKLES)

2293
01:55:30.799 --> 01:55:32.232
Unbelievable.

2294
01:55:35.870 --> 01:55:37.371
(CHUCKLING)

2295
01:55:45.145 --> 01:55:46.714
Uh... Oh, boy.

2296
01:56:11.940 --> 01:56:13.207
(CHUCKLING)

2297
01:56:14.642 --> 01:56:15.976
Amazing.

2298
01:56:22.717 --> 01:56:24.017
See you, guys.

2299
01:56:28.556 --> 01:56:31.225
<i>(MAKE THE WORLD GO AWAY</i>
CONTINUES PLAYING)

2300
01:56:31.325 --> 01:56:33.293
(ENGINE TURNS OVER, WHIRRING)

2301
01:57:04.091 --> 01:57:06.026
(SONG ENDS)

2302
01:57:06.126 --> 01:57:08.262
<i>(LIMELIGHT</i> BY THE ALAN PARSONS
PROJECT PLAYING)

2303
02:01:43.303 --> 02:01:45.673
(HARP MUSIC PLAYING)

2304
02:03:01.381 --> 02:03:03.751
(MUSIC FADES OUT)
